{#
contacts/_pane_layout.html.twig — a contacts page inside the pane docked beside
the mail. Chosen by contacts/_layout.html.twig; see there for when.

Only the frame: Turbo takes the matching <turbo-frame> out of the response and
swaps it into the pane, so a topbar and a sidebar would be built for nothing.

Its way out to the full page and its close button are in each page's own
header — _pane_actions.html.twig — rather than a bar above it, which would
only have said "Contacts" over a header that already says it.
#}

<turbo-frame id="contacts-pane-frame" class="flex flex-col min-h-0 flex-1">
    {# The flashes a save leaves ("Contact created."). The full layout renders
       them into the toast region; this one has no toast region of its own, so
       it sends them there as streams, which Turbo runs as they land in the
       page. Read here, so the bag is cleared and they do not turn up again on
       the next full page. #}
    {% for type, messages in app.flashes(['success', 'error', 'info']) %}
        {% for message in messages %}
            {% include '_partials/_toast.stream.html.twig' with { message: message, type: type } only %}
        {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}

    {# data-contacts-page: content, so contacts--pane knows this frame needs
       no src to fill it. #}
    <div data-contacts-page class="@container relative flex flex-col flex-1 min-h-0 min-w-0 overflow-hidden">
        {% block contacts_content %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
</turbo-frame>
